<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- CHANGED 3 Oct 2026 - one size for all ten, and a sortable label.

     The label is what the launcher sorts on, so the three Quick Add widgets
     share a "Quick Add: " prefix to keep them clustered instead of scattered
     alphabetically. That is a real fix for "the order is cluttered", and it is
     also why the Quick Add labels gained a colon: without a common prefix
     "Contact"/"Encounter"/"Medication" sort by their own first letter.

     min/targetCell are now IDENTICAL across all ten, because a picker offering
     four different footprints reads as cluttered even when each size is
     individually correct. maxResize still varies where the content genuinely
     needs it - that is the cap that stops the empty-black-box growth, which is
     a different concern from the size the picker offers.

     CHANGED 16 Oct 2026 (t116) - maxResizeWidth 180dp -> 530dp. It was EQUAL to
     minWidth, which is not a cap but a prohibition: the horizontal resize range
     was empty, so a widget could never be dragged wider than the width the
     fitter is fitted for, and the user had no lever at all. Every truncation
     here is width-driven - measured on 23124RA7EO, the same string breaks
     mid-word at 109dp and renders complete at 171dp. 530dp is Google's own
     figure for a 3x2 widget; their samples declare 624dp and never a max equal
     to the min. maxResizeHeight is deliberately UNCHANGED: the empty black box it
     prevents is a real reported defect, and a wider widget does not worsen it.
     Note an XML comment cannot sit inside a start tag, which is why this note
     lives up here. Full reasoning in CLAUDE.md and docs/HISTORY.md. -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:label="Cycle"
    android:description="@string/widget_desc_cycle"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="100dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="80dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="530dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="220dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/cycle_widget"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/cycle_widget"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview_cycle"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
